#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:113
msgid ""
"*scale*\\ [**+a**\\ *angle*][**+f**\\ *font*][**+j**\\ *justify*] [**+l**]"
"[**+m**][**+o**\\ *dx*\\ [/\\ *dy*]][**+s**\\ *reference*]. Adjust scaling "
"of the radius of the beachball, which is  proportional to the magnitude. By "
"default, *scale* defines the size for magnitude = 5 (i.e., scalar seismic "
"moment M0 = 4.0E23 dyn cm). If **+l** is used the radius will be "
"proportional to the seismic moment instead. Use **+s** and give a "
"*reference* to change the reference magnitude (or moment), and use **+m** to "
"plot all beachballs with the same size. A text string can be specified to "
"appear near the beachball (corresponding to column or parameter "
"``event_name``). Append **+a**\\ *angle* to change the angle of the text "
"string; append **+f**\\ *font* to change its font (size,fontname,color); "
"append **+j**\\ *justify* to change the text location relative to the "
"beachball [Default is ``\"TC\"``, i.e., Top Center]; append **+o** to offset "
"the text string by *dx*\\ /*dy*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:128
msgid ""
"Specify the focal mechanism convention of the input data. Ignored if "
"``spec`` is a dict or :class:`pandas.DataFrame`. See the table above for the "
"supported conventions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:132
msgid ""
"The component of the seismic moment tensor to plot. Valid values are:  - "
"``\"full\"``: the full seismic moment tensor - ``\"dc\"``: the closest "
"double couple defined from the moment tensor (zero trace   and zero "
"determinant) - ``\"deviatoric\"``: deviatoric part of the moment tensor "
"(zero trace)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:132
msgid "The component of the seismic moment tensor to plot. Valid values are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:134
msgid "``\"full\"``: the full seismic moment tensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:135
msgid ""
"``\"dc\"``: the closest double couple defined from the moment tensor (zero "
"trace and zero determinant)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:137
msgid "``\"deviatoric\"``: deviatoric part of the moment tensor (zero trace)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:138
msgid ""
"Longitude(s), latitude(s), and depth(s) of the event(s). The length of each "
"must match the number of events. These parameters are only used if ``spec`` "
"is a dictionary or a :class:`pandas.DataFrame`, and they override any "
"existing ``longitude``, ``latitude``, or ``depth`` values in ``spec``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:142
msgid ""
"Longitude(s) and latitude(s) at which to place the beachball(s). The length "
"of each must match the number of events. These parameters are only used if "
"``spec`` is a dictionary or a :class:`pandas.DataFrame`, and they override "
"any existing ``plot_longitude`` or ``plot_latitude`` values in ``spec``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:147
msgid ""
"Text string(s), such as event name(s), to appear near the beachball(s). The "
"length must match the number of events. This parameter is only used if "
"``spec`` is a dictionary or a :class:`pandas.DataFrame`, and it overrides "
"any existing ``event_name`` labels in ``spec``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:151
msgid ""
"[*fill*]. Draw a box behind the label if given via ``event_name``. Use "
"*fill* to give a fill color [Default is ``\"white\"``]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:155
msgid ""
"[**+p**\\ *pen*][**+s**\\ *size*]. Offset beachball(s) to the longitude(s) "
"and latitude(s) specified in the last two columns of the input file or "
"array, or by ``plot_longitude`` and ``plot_latitude`` if provided. A line "
"from the beachball to the initial location is drawn. Use **+s**\\ *size* to "
"plot a small circle at the initial location and to set the diameter of this "
"circle [Default is no circle]. Use **+p**\\ *pen* to set the pen attributes "
"for this feature [Default is set via ``pen``]. The fill of the circle is set "
"via ``compression_fill`` or ``cmap``, i.e., corresponds to the fill of the "
"compressive quadrants."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:166
msgid ""
"Set color or pattern for filling compressive quadrants [Default is "
"``\"black\"``]. This setting also applies to the fill of the circle defined "
"via ``offset``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:169
msgid ""
"Set color or pattern for filling extensive quadrants [Default is "
"``\"white\"``]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:171
msgid ""
"Set (default) pen attributes for all lines related to the beachball [Default "
"is ``\"0.25p,black,solid\"``]. This setting applies to ``outline``, "
"``nodal``, and ``offset``, unless overruled by arguments passed to those "
"parameters. Draws the circumference of the beachball."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:175
msgid ""
"[*pen*]. Draw circumference and nodal planes of the beachball. Use *pen* to "
"set  the pen attributes for this feature [Default is set via ``pen``]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:179
msgid ""
"[*nplane*][/*pen*]. Plot the nodal planes and outline the bubble which is "
"transparent. If *nplane* is  - ``0`` or ``True``: both nodal planes are "
"plotted [Default]. - ``1``: only the first nodal plane is plotted. - ``2``: "
"only the second nodal plane is plotted.  Use /*pen* to set the pen "
"attributes for this feature [Default is set via ``pen``]. For double couple "
"mechanisms, ``nodal`` renders the beachball transparent by drawing only the "
"nodal planes and the circumference. For non-double couple mechanisms, "
"``nodal=0`` overlays best double couple transparently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:179
msgid ""
"[*nplane*][/*pen*]. Plot the nodal planes and outline the bubble which is "
"transparent. If *nplane* is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:183
msgid "``0`` or ``True``: both nodal planes are plotted [Default]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:184
msgid "``1``: only the first nodal plane is plotted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:185
msgid "``2``: only the second nodal plane is plotted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:187
msgid ""
"Use /*pen* to set the pen attributes for this feature [Default is set via "
"``pen``]. For double couple mechanisms, ``nodal`` renders the beachball "
"transparent by drawing only the nodal planes and the circumference. For non-"
"double couple mechanisms, ``nodal=0`` overlays best double couple "
"transparently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:194
msgid ""
"File name of a CPT file or a series of comma-separated colors (e.g., *color1,"
"color2,color3*) to build a linear continuous CPT from those colors "
"automatically. The color of the compressive quadrants is determined by the z-"
"value (i.e., event depth or the third column for an input file). This "
"setting also applies to the fill of the circle defined via ``offset``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:200
msgid ""
"Do **not** skip symbols that fall outside the frame boundaries [Default is "
"``False``, i.e., plot symbols inside the frame boundaries only]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:203
msgid ""
"*projcode*\\[*projparams*/]\\ *width*\\|\\ *scale*. Select map :doc:"
"`projection </projections/index>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:205
msgid ""
"[*xmin*, *xmax*, *ymin*, *ymax*] or *xmin/xmax/ymin/ymax*\\ [**+r**]"
"[**+u**\\ *unit*]. Specify the :doc:`region </tutorials/basics/regions>` of "
"interest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:210
msgid ""
"Set frame and axes attributes for the plot. It can be a bool, ``\"none\"``, "
"a :class:`pygmt.params.Frame` or :class:`pygmt.params.Axis` object. Raw GMT "
"strings or sequences of strings are also supported for backward "
"compatibility. If ``frame=True``, the frame will be drawn with the default "
"attributes. If ``frame=\"none\"``, no frame will be drawn. Use a :class:"
"`pygmt.params.Frame` or :class:`pygmt.params.Axis` object for more control "
"over the attributes of the frame and axes. A tutorial is available at :doc:"
"`frame and axes attributes </tutorials/basics/frames>`. Full documentation "
"is at :gmt-docs:`gmt.html#b-full`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:219
msgid "Select verbosity level [:term:`Full usage <verbose>`]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:222
msgid ""
"Select a specific subplot panel. Only allowed when used in :meth:`Figure."
"subplot` mode.  - ``True`` to advance to the next panel in the selected "
"order. - *index* to specify the index of the desired panel. - (*row*, *col*) "
"to specify the row and column of the desired panel.  The panel order is "
"determined by the :meth:`Figure.subplot` method. *row*, *col* and *index* "
"all start at 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:222
msgid ""
"Select a specific subplot panel. Only allowed when used in :meth:`Figure."
"subplot` mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:225
msgid "``True`` to advance to the next panel in the selected order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:226
msgid "*index* to specify the index of the desired panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:227
msgid "(*row*, *col*) to specify the row and column of the desired panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:229
msgid ""
"The panel order is determined by the :meth:`Figure.subplot` method. *row*, "
"*col* and *index* all start at 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:232
msgid ""
"Select perspective view and set the azimuth and elevation of the viewpoint.  "
"Accepts a single value or a sequence of two or three values: *azimuth*, "
"(*azimuth*, *elevation*), or (*azimuth*, *elevation*, *zlevel*).  - "
"*azimuth*: Azimuth angle of the viewpoint in degrees [Default is 180,   i."
"e., looking from south to north]. - *elevation*: Elevation angle of the "
"viewpoint above the horizon [Default   is 90, i.e., looking straight down at "
"nadir]. - *zlevel*: Z-level at which 2-D elements (e.g., the plot frame) are "
"drawn.   Only applied when used together with ``zsize`` or ``zscale``. "
"[Default is   at the bottom of the z-axis].  Alternatively, set "
"``perspective=True`` to reuse the perspective setting from the previous "
"plotting method, or pass a string following the full GMT syntax for finer "
"control (e.g., adding ``+w`` or ``+v`` modifiers to select an axis location "
"other than the plot origin). See :gmt-docs:`gmt.html#perspective-full` for "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:232
msgid ""
"Select perspective view and set the azimuth and elevation of the viewpoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:234
msgid ""
"Accepts a single value or a sequence of two or three values: *azimuth*, "
"(*azimuth*, *elevation*), or (*azimuth*, *elevation*, *zlevel*)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:237
msgid ""
"*azimuth*: Azimuth angle of the viewpoint in degrees [Default is 180, i.e., "
"looking from south to north]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:239
msgid ""
"*elevation*: Elevation angle of the viewpoint above the horizon [Default is "
"90, i.e., looking straight down at nadir]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:241
msgid ""
"*zlevel*: Z-level at which 2-D elements (e.g., the plot frame) are drawn. "
"Only applied when used together with ``zsize`` or ``zscale``. [Default is at "
"the bottom of the z-axis]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:245
msgid ""
"Alternatively, set ``perspective=True`` to reuse the perspective setting "
"from the previous plotting method, or pass a string following the full GMT "
"syntax for finer control (e.g., adding ``+w`` or ``+v`` modifiers to select "
"an axis location other than the plot origin). See :gmt-docs:`gmt."
"html#perspective-full` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/meca.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.meca.meca:250
msgid ""
"Set transparency level, in [0-100] percent range [Default is ``0``, i.e., "
"opaque]. Only visible when PDF or raster format output is selected. Only the "
"PNG format selection adds a transparency layer in the image (for further "
"processing)."
msgstr ""

